pr_comments:
@ywang96 I totally agree that we can import the `Attention` implementation from `transformers`, since most of ViTs have implemented their `SDPA` and `FlashAttention` there. This can prevent duplicated implementation.

`InternViT` may be an exception for this, because they haven't added their models to `transformers` yet, but seems that they have had a plan for this (see [here](https://huggingface.co/OpenGVLab/InternVL2-1B/discussions/3)). And we may need to add a sdpa implementation for it manually.

However, one potential tricky point is that the `FlashAttention2` implemented in `transformers` is not compatible with `vllm` because it requires `flash_attn` instead of `vllm_flash_attn`. And it also doesn't support tensor parallel as well. As a result, if we want to use flash attention to speed up the encoder inference in the future, we may need to re-implement it. (Please correct me if I'm misunderstanding wrong).

@ywang96 I also add a `transformers` attention fallback when tensor parallel unavailable (`num_heads` can't be divided by `tp_size`). 

IMO, TP on ViT shouldn't block user to use a larger tp size, especially it doesn't bring as much performance benefit as on backbone.

For example, InternViT with `num_attention_heads=25` mentioned in https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/8055#issuecomment-2324052980, TP on ViT is blocking user to apply `tp_size=4` or higher for large model inference currently.
